# The CUDA home's kernel bodies, its emitter and its lens are written at the engine's width, the
# width dasLLAMA's stamps and cells take: a kernel body's width is the stamp's, never the gate's.
# Both measures are unchecked here until the sweep followup_general.md row 213 names wraps the
# tree; then this file goes and the repo limits bind.
[line_length]
